-| Input on a standalone pin | Action |
+In the editor, `P` or `Ctrl+P` stores a pin in the lower-right stack.
+`omasnap --pin-clipboard` adds the current clipboard image to the same stack.
+Each monitor has its own stack, visible across workspaces. Cards show a
+thumbnail of the complete image. Detached images keep their proportions and
+large captures fit the work area.
+
+| Input | Action |
 |---|---|
-| Drag the image | Move the pin |
-| Wheel / `Alt`+wheel | Zoom by 10% / 1% |
-| `Ctrl`+wheel | Change opacity by 5% |
-| Middle-click | Restore original size, fitted to the work area if needed |
-| Double-click / `Esc` / `X` | Close the pin |
+| Click the folded stack | Expand the cards |
+| Click an expanded card | Open the image in the center of the work area |
+| Drag a card or detached image | Move it to any position |
+| Drag the lower-right grip of a detached image | Resize at the original aspect ratio |
+| Right-click a detached image | Return to stack, delete, or access image actions |
+| Right-click a stacked card | Collapse the stack or access image actions |
+| `Esc` / `X` while focused | Delete the pin |
+| Double-click a detached image | Delete the pin |
+| Wheel / `Alt`+wheel on a detached image | Zoom by 10% / 1% |
+| `Ctrl`+wheel on a detached image | Change opacity by 5% |
+| Middle-click on a detached image | Restore original size, fitted to the work area if needed |
 | `Shift`+drag | Drag the full PNG into a file-capable drop target |
 | `A` / `E` while hovered | Edit the pin |
 | `Ctrl+C` | Copy the full image |
